// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'databaseName'. Valid alternatives: ['clusterID', 'endpointURL', 'region', 'name', 'host', 'port']
//
// `databaseName:` on a Redshift specification, which spells the database `name`. The word
// `databaseName` is not invented -- it is MemSql's spelling for the same concept, in the same
// `###Connection` section, three lines of grammar away.
//
// Across this batch the database is called `name` (Redshift, Aurora, Static), `databaseName`
// (MemSql), `database` (Athena), `databaseId` (Spanner), `defaultDataset` (BigQuery),
// `serviceName` (Oracle), `path` (DuckDB) and `catalog`+`schema` (Trino). Nine grammars, nine
// answers, and each lexer declares its own token rather than importing a shared one -- so the
// name is not a synonym a parser may resolve, it is the only key that exists.
//
// The alternative list is Redshift's complete surface; the sibling fixtures
// ./neg-oracle-name-not-servicename.pure, ./neg-duckdb-name-not-path.pure and
// ./neg-databricks-host-not-hostname.pure pin three more points of the same map.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::RedshiftDatabaseName
{
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  type: Redshift;
  specification: Redshift
  {
    databaseName: 'db';
    host: 'h';
    port: 1234;
  };
  auth: Test;
}
